---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Button from '@/components/Button.astro';

const credentials = [
  'Bilingual English/Spanish content strategist and writer based in Madrid',
  'A decade of professional content and thought leadership experience across fintech and SaaS, including Ria Money Transfer, Dandelion Payments, and Sketch',
  "Author of The Currency of Caring, a 72-page proprietary research study on the human side of remittances and the most ambitious thought leadership project in Ria's history",
  'Content lead and on-camera interviewer for Good Teacher, a documentary produced in partnership with Save the Children, a documentary that won two Cannes Corporate Media & TV Awards and a Silver Trophy at the New York Festivals TV & Film Awards',
  'Founder and lead writer of The World We Share, an ongoing storytelling series now embedded in onboarding, sales, and partner relationships across the company',
  'Developed thought leadership content for industry events including Sibos and Money 20/20',
  "Bylined case study writer for Sketch, one of the world's leading B2B design platforms",
  'Dual BA in Creative Writing and Communications, Manhattanville University',
  'MA in Hispanic Literature, Art, History & Society, Universidad Autónoma de Madrid',
  'Certified creative writing instructor, Escuela de Escritores, Madrid',
  'Founder of Cajón de garabatos, a bilingual literary newsletter on writing, reading, and creativity',
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Gabrielle van Welie, bilingual content strategist and writer in Madrid, and the voice behind Phren Thought Studio."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-16 pb-24 sm:pt-24">
    <p class="text-ink-soft mb-6 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em] uppercase">About me</p>

    <h1 class="font-display text-ink max-w-xl text-3xl font-medium sm:text-4xl">
      I’m Gabrielle, the voice behind Phren Thought Studio.
    </h1>

    <div class="prose prose-sm sm:prose-base mt-8 max-w-xl">
      <p>
        When I told my parents I was going to major in creative writing, they did what any sensible
        parent would do: urge me to at least double-major in something that could actually get me a
        job. Now, after a decade of professional content experience, I’m glad I stuck with creative
        writing.
      </p>
      <p>
        The internet has become a place where words are cheap, and often generated, resulting in a
        sea of meaninglessness where all brands sound the same. Yes. I can write with a sense of
        urgency to coax some algorithm. Because it’s not about prose, it’s about closing deals. But
        I’m more interested in what makes businesses actually thrive: human connection.
      </p>
      <p>
        Careful storytelling is an essential tool for any brand. Expert thought leadership can help
        bring the clarity your business needs or help you build trust with the people who truly
        resonate with your offering.
      </p>
      <p>
        And maybe there are a lot of people or generative tools that promise to build you just the
        right content for just the right audience. But I believe truly impactful thought leadership
        can’t be built from templates or pattern-predicting technologies. You and your business are
        unique, both in your essence and in your challenges. And so am I.
      </p>
      <p>
        Writing something out is the least of your worries. The problem is finding what goes onto
        the page. Did you drift away from your value proposition? Do you have less proprietary data
        than you thought you would? I help you answer the hard questions so we can build something
        together that is true to you, your business, and the customers and collaborators that are
        still waiting for the chance to come on board.
      </p>
      <p>That’s my story, but there are plenty of credentials to go with it:</p>
    </div>

    <ul class="mt-8 max-w-2xl">
      {
        credentials.map((c) => (
          <li class="border-line text-ink-soft grid grid-cols-[1.25rem_1fr] gap-2 border-b py-3 text-sm sm:text-base">
            <span class="text-signal" aria-hidden="true">—</span>
            <span>{c}</span>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>

    <Button href="/contact" class="mt-10">Begin the conversation →</Button>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
